        {
          "id": 2073608282,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> I think @geraldcombs usually takes the approach of creating a file that can be sourced that creates an environment variable in the container, so that the the CI file doesn't have to change on every branch when the container does (and prevents having to revert).\n\nThat's all done in https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark-containers/-/blob/master/development/ubuntu/Dockerfile. I'll push a change to add gcc-14 and g++-14. It looks like it's going to add another ~1.1GB to our image. Hopefully we can start trimming things off at some point.\n\n> the `wireshark-containers` job doesn't automatically run after commits (only quarterly)\n\nThe image versions increment each quarter, but they're built each Sunday. That should probably be more clear in the README.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
